{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1396691-silent-sound-artifact-for-review","id":1396691,"title":"Silent Sound - Artifact for review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-15T10:22:06-07:00","id":1396691,"title":"Silent Sound - Artifact for review","content":"I came up with this Artifact for one of my players, but am new to evocations in Exalted 3e, and was wondering whether it looked ok.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Silent Sound</b><br /> <b>Moonsilver and Blue Jade Flute/Short Daiklaive (Artifact 4)</b><br /> In the cold of winter, in the far North, a small community existed, living inside a cave, where the howling winds outside wouldn\u2019t enter. Living off lichen and moss that grew abundant in the cave, the people of that small community lived a meager, but good, life, considering the situation outside. But one day, a group of Dragon-Blooded came, and seeing the Blue Jade in the cave, began to systematically dismantle it, despite the protests of the inhabitants. And so, stripped of its blue Jade, the cave couldn\u2019t deaden the sounds of the howling winds, and when one of the Dragon-Blooded came back, she found them all dead.<br /> Ailera Twice-Sounding was beset by remorse. And wandered the cave to see if there was something she could do, when she found out a little girl who survived, hiding quietly. From her she learned of the Fae who came in, making all sorts of raucous, and killing anyone who made a sound. After telling her story, the little girl died, and in her little hand, was a small piece of Blue Jade, mixed with Moonsilver. Intrigued by this, Ailera found a small place where the two magical materials seemed to blend.<br /> She turned the cave into a forge, and began to work on a flute to commemorate the place. But every night, the Fae came, with their howling, and she had to adjust the flute to also serve as a weapon, to be used against them. And so, for 10 years she labored by day, and fought by night. Until finally, she quenched the finished flute in the gossamer of the Raksha who came to see who was it that had held off his minions for so long every night.<br /> Rumors say that Ailera herself was struck mute in that battle, her voice taken from her, though others speculate that she gave up her voice to invest it into Silent Sound. A few claim that she became a monk afterwards.<br /> <b>Evocations</b><br /> A Lunar or Dragon-Blooded attuned to Silent Sound gains +1 non-charm die to Social rolls that do not involve using your voice.<br /> <br /> <b>Silent Sheath</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m: <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Action<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> None<br /> As you harmonize with the flute, its silence envelops you. Those who try to find you using their sense of hearing suffer a -2 penalty to such checks, as your sounds fade to the background.<br /> <br /> <b>Silence is a Weapon</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Silent Sheath<br /> While created as a flute, it\u2019s creator had to use it as a weapon against those who sought to interrupt her, and so, remembering that time, the flute can be changed into a short daiklaive.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sound of Silence</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m, 2i; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute, Withering-Only<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Action<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Silence is a Weapon<br /> As your connection with the silence within the weapon deepens, you can extend this \u2018blessing\u2019 to your opponents, rendering them unable to scream, or shout, or otherwise blow your presence.<br /> An opponent struck must make a Stamina + Resistance check or be silent for one action, with a difficulty of Wielder\u2019s Essence + Successes on the attack. The attack would inflict only half the normal raw damage.<br /> <br /> <b>On Silent Wings</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1 wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Silent Sheath<br /> Drawing the silence of the Artifact around you, you create a veil that hides you from the world. You gain a +2 non-charm die to all Stealth rolls, and can reroll all 5s until no 5s appear. The effect ends if you make an attack.<br /> <br /> <b>A Silent Lullaby</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 10m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Action<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> The Sound of Silence, On Silent Wings<br /> This charm can only be used when Silent Sound is in flute form, as it requires playing it to keep the effect going. When playing correctly, it can mask the presence of you, and your allies.<br /> Make a Manipulation + Performance check. Anyone whose Resolve is lower than your roll will ignore you as if he did not hear or see you, or a number of allies up to Essence*5. You and your allies can take other actions while under this effect, though it takes a reflexive action to maintain the effect. the charm ends its effect on anyone who rolls join Battle, or takes an overt action that draws attention to herself, like brandishing a weapon. If you do either of those, or stop playing the music, the effect ends for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","user":"Greyskull","date":". 06-16-2020, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T16:28:16-07:00","id":1396744,"title":"","content":"These Evocations are definitely way too weak. Your capstone is worse than an essence 1 dragon-blooded charm with no prerequisites that does the same thing for only a fifth of the cost.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T00:32:41-07:00","id":1396830,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. because it's my first Artifact, I'd rather err on the side of weak, and increase the power from there. i improved the last two Evocations, and would love more feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/721-greyskull","name":"Greyskull","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-17T06:17:39-07:00","id":1397076,"title":"","content":"&quot;Easily Overlooked Presence Method but my friends can come too&quot; is an ok effect for essence 3 I guess, but I'm still not sure if it's worth 10m1w. Plus if you're gonna write &quot;this effect but AoE&quot; then you might as well just make the original a prerequisite. Evocations with Charm prerequisites are a thing for a reason. You should also probably include a range for the effect or something.<br /> <br /> I still would never ever use On Silent Wings, much less spend a turn on activating it. It turns itself off when you attack (why?) so it's useless for combat (outside maybe turtling with Stalkiing Wolf Attitude and missing the entire fight) and outside of combat I'm basically never expecting to make enough stealth rolls for this to pay itself off so I'd rather save my willpower for something else.<br /> <br /> Why not add any Resonant/Dissonant keywords? That might help you hit the ballpark of power rather than lowballing everything. Unless you don't want to bother, which is fine for a one-off artifact, but you've told us nothing about what character this is for so judging whether it's appropriate is basically guesswork. I still don't even get what you intended this artifact to be, a social thing, a stealth thing, a combat thing? all of the above? The attunement effect says the first but everything else says the second. Except it's also a sword. I'd advise against cramming too many roles into a single artifact like this.<br /> <br /> Related, what makes you think this is a 4 dot artifact? I'm seeing a low 3 on both the power and weirdness scales.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}